Why Apache-2.0 rather than a copyleft or source-available licence:

Running Saathi yourself — on your own machine, against your own model, with your
own key or none at all — is the primary objective, and every restriction is a
reason for someone not to. Schools, disability organisations and universities are
exactly the adopters an accessibility tool wants, and they are also the ones whose
legal review stops at an unfamiliar licence. Apache-2.0 over MIT for the explicit
patent grant, which those same organisations ask about.

There is a hosted service, and it is not protected by withholding code. It runs
the same backend in this repository, with accounts and metering switched on by
configuration. What it sells is not having to run or configure anything.
